			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Align FileSystemProviderError names with VS Code's token format\n\nWind's FileSystemErrorCode uses key-like values ('FileNotFound', 'FileExists'), but VS Code's toFileSystemProviderErrorCode extracts the token from error.name and switches on 'EntryNotFound', 'EntryExists', etc. Add a mapping function VsCodeErrorCodeToken to translate between the two formats.\n\nAlso set this.name to the '<code> (FileSystemError)' pattern that VS Code's markAsFileSystemProviderError() expects. Remove individual name assignments from subclasses since the base class now handles naming.\n\nWithout this fix, mkdirp and validateWriteFile treat missing-file/dir errors as unknown and rethrow, surfacing as unhandled rejections like 'Unable to write file .../tasks.log (Error: Failed to stat file ...)'.",
			"SHA": "4e2e6bdf2faa8cad9556c62d1788a1c34b9ebf4b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T00:28:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Correct userDataSync channel names in IPC stubs\n\nThe previous commit used incorrect IPC channel names for the userDataSync stubs:\n- `userDataSyncService` renamed to `userDataSync` (matches workbench/services/userDataSync/electron-browser/userDataSyncService.ts:13)\n- `userDataSync` renamed to `userDataSyncAccount` (matches userDataSyncIpc.ts:51)\n\nThe channel names now align with the actual VS Code IPC registration, ensuring calls route to the correct stub handlers.",
			"SHA": "671d83254b54b385da95e4e12d8acd7ec4d995e3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T23:24:34Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Add IPC stubs for unimplemented VS Code services\n\nSeveral VS Code services invoked at runtime lack Mountain-side implementations,\ncausing IPC calls to return undefined. Downstream code then crashes when\nattempting operations like .forEach(), .map(), or destructuring on undefined.\n\nAdd stub handlers in TauriMainProcessService for:\n- extensionTipsService: Return empty arrays for recommendation queries\n- mcpManagement/mcpWorkbenchManagement: Return empty arrays for server lists\n- userDataSyncService: Return 'Uninitialised' status tuple [0, [], null]\n- userDataSync: Return undefined for account/not-signed-in state\n- userDataSyncStoreManagement: Return null\n- userDataAutoSync: Return undefined for trigger/turnOn/turnOff\n- languageDetection: Return null and empty extensions for detection\n\nThese stubs match the absence of corresponding backends in Land while\npreventing crashes in VS Code code paths that expect valid return shapes.",
			"SHA": "f0d6ccbe685fb74c28b788eedfd5533be49afb03"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1778513324644
}